  "_readme": [
    "T-204 - the 409 `denial_reason` parser, ONE table read by both languages.",
    "",
    "GENERATED, never hand-written: every `code` here is the answer",
    "`exchange.accept.reasons.denial_code` gives for that `reason`, and",
    "`test_denial_vocabulary.py::test_every_corpus_row_is_what_the_exchanges_own_parser_answers`",
    "re-derives all of them, so a row cannot be edited to match a broken consumer.",
    "`denial_vocabulary.test.ts` drives `contracts/ts/vocabulary.ts::denialCode` with the",
    "same file.",
    "",
    "The rows that matter are the blank ones. The exchange strips the token with Python's",
    "`str.strip()`; a TypeScript client reaching for `trim()` disagrees in both directions -",
    "`trim()` keeps U+001C-U+001F and U+0085, which Python removes, and removes U+FEFF,",
    "which Python keeps. Each of those is a row here, so a hand-rolled parser fails the",
    "suite instead of failing a buyer."
